1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:05,550
After an early morning wake up the first thing we did was to head to our other must do attraction here.
一早起床后，我们首先去了这里另一个必体验的景点。

2
00:00:05,550 --> 00:00:12,570
The thermae bath spa is the only place in britain where you can bathe in naturally warm mineral rich waters.
作者介绍，Thermae Bath Spa 是英国唯一能泡天然温暖、富含矿物质泉水的地方。

3
00:00:12,570 --> 00:00:15,720
You obviously can't take any photos beyond the changing rooms.
更衣室以后的区域，显然不能拍照。

4
00:00:15,720 --> 00:00:19,850
So I want to thank thermae bath spa for letting me use some of their footage here.
所以，我要感谢 Thermae Bath Spa，让我在这里使用他们的一些影像。

5
00:00:19,850 --> 00:00:24,180
First you get given a smart band which doubles up as your locker key.
首先，你会拿到一条智能腕带，它同时也充当储物柜钥匙。

6
00:00:24,180 --> 00:00:29,949
And allows any further charges such as food to be loaded onto them to pay later.
其他消费，比如餐饮，也可以记在腕带上，之后再付。

7
00:00:29,959 --> 00:00:36,199
You start in the minerva bath the largest of all the baths here complete with massage jets and whirlpools.
先进入的是 Minerva 浴池，它是这里最大的浴池，配有按摩喷嘴和漩涡水流。

8
00:00:36,199 --> 00:00:41,779
We then made our way to the wellness suite which is probably the most sophisticated one I have ever been in.
接着我们去了康养区，它大概是我去过的同类区域里最精致的一处。

9
00:00:41,779 --> 00:00:47,779
They have steam rooms infrared rooms and an ice chamber which is as cold as it sounds.
那里有蒸汽房、红外线房，还有冰室；后者真就像名字听起来那么冷。

10
00:00:47,779 --> 00:00:51,079
And we ended in the celestial relaxation room.
最后，我们去了“天体放松室”。

11
00:00:51,079 --> 00:00:57,279
Here you lie in a darkened space room as if you were a naughty neil armstrong on his day off.
你在昏暗、太空主题的房间里躺下，仿佛自己是休假中的“淘气版尼尔·阿姆斯特朗”。

12
00:00:57,279 --> 00:01:02,579
All of which helped make this entire floor a completely unique experience.
这些体验，让这一整层都变成了非常独特的体验空间。

13
00:01:02,589 --> 00:01:12,409
Similar to the original roman baths just a stone's throw away the main attraction here is the open air pool situated on the rooftop with an overlooking bath abbey.
就像近在咫尺的古罗马浴场一样，这里的主要看点是屋顶露天泳池，还可以俯瞰巴斯修道院。

14
00:01:12,409 --> 00:01:16,949
This is about as close as a roman bathing experience as you can get.
这大概已经是你能获得的、最接近罗马人泡澡的体验了。

15
00:01:16,959 --> 00:01:23,019
Enhanced by air seats and bubbling jets it was probably my weekend highlight and a must visit.
再加上气泡座位和冒泡喷嘴，这大概是我周末最精彩的体验，也是我认为必去的一站。

16
00:01:23,019 --> 00:01:32,110
It can get very busy here especially on the weekends but it never felt overcrowded since they managed how many people are in the space at one single time.
这里尤其在周末会很忙，但从没觉得过度拥挤，因为他们会控制同一时间的入场人数。

17
00:01:32,110 --> 00:01:37,749
We actually walked past the day before to see long wait times which is why we came back the next day.
其实我们前一天路过时看到要等很久，所以第二天才回来。

18
00:01:37,749 --> 00:01:42,319
Joining the queue at 9 00 a m we were in around 45 minutes later.
我们早上九点加入队伍，大约四十五分钟后进去了。

19
00:01:42,319 --> 00:01:51,629
If you are interested I would recommend checking out their website for more details which again I have linked below in the description.
感兴趣的话，作者建议到官网查看详情；链接同样放在下方的视频说明里。

20
00:01:51,639 --> 00:02:00,969
After all of that floating our stomachs needed some brunch we ended up at the boston tea party which was exactly what the doctor ordered for a sunday morning.
漂浮了那么久，我们的肚子需要些早午餐；最后去了 Boston Tea Party，这正是周日早晨所需要的。

21
00:02:00,979 --> 00:02:09,749
Oh and also everyone at some point in their life needs to sample a full english breakfast lovely.
还有，每个人一生中总得找个时候尝尝全套英式早餐。真不错。

22
00:02:09,759 --> 00:02:16,329
We still had around four and a half hours to explore this compact city with three things remaining on our to do list.
我们还剩大约四个半小时探索这座紧凑的城市，待办清单上有三件事。

23
00:02:16,339 --> 00:02:21,559
We decided to drop off our bags at a left luggage spot right in front of bath spa station.
我们决定把行李寄存在巴斯温泉车站正前方的行李寄存点。

24
00:02:21,559 --> 00:02:26,619
This only costs a few pounds and made things much easier for our eventual return back to london.
作者那次寄存只花几英镑，也让我们之后返回伦敦轻松多了。

25
00:02:26,629 --> 00:02:29,839
As mentioned bath is a perfect place for walking.
前面也提过，巴斯非常适合步行。

26
00:02:29,839 --> 00:02:38,709
The fact that the city itself is a world heritage site gives weight to the places you will undoubtedly bump into on foot.
这座城市本身就是世界遗产地，这让你走路时必然会遇见的那些地方，更添了一份分量。

27
00:02:38,709 --> 00:02:42,559
Pulteney bridge was built in the 1700 s crossing the river avon.
作者介绍，普尔特尼桥建于十八世纪，横跨埃文河。

28
00:02:42,559 --> 00:02:48,759
It is one of only four bridges in the world that houses shops for its full span on either side.
据作者说，它是世界上仅有的四座、桥的两侧从头到尾都有商店的桥之一。

29
00:02:48,759 --> 00:02:53,369
The three other bridges are in erfurt germany venice and florence.
另外三座桥，分别在德国埃尔福特、威尼斯和佛罗伦萨。

30
00:02:53,379 --> 00:03:03,249
Which at this point provides a great opportunity to say that if you're enjoying this vlog please also check out our tuscany video where you can see that bridge in action.
说到这里，正好借机说一句：如果你喜欢这段视频，也看看我们的托斯卡纳视频，在那里能看到那座桥的实际画面。

31
00:03:03,249 --> 00:03:13,299
The shops lining the bridge themselves are very narrow which even span two floors giving you a unique view looking out onto the river.
桥边的店铺本身很狭窄，有的还分成两层，让你能从独特的角度望向河面。

32
00:03:13,299 --> 00:03:18,499
As our hours in bath counted down we headed northwest.
在巴斯的剩余时间越来越少，我们朝西北方向走去。

33
00:03:18,499 --> 00:03:27,169
Here you will find some of bath's best examples of georgian architecture including the circus as well as the impressively large royal crescent.
在这里，能看到巴斯一些最出色的乔治时期建筑，包括圆形广场，以及规模令人印象深刻的皇家新月楼。
